  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full test suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Cause:** when `Context` creates a subcommand's context, it copied the parent's whole `default_map` to the child. It should have used only the entry under the subcommand's name. So `{\"sub\": {\"name\": \"x\"}}` was looked up for `name` at the top level and never found.\n\n**Fix:** `src/click/core.py:392` now reads `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It invokes a group with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` and checks that the subcommand's option gets `mapped`.",
